<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 63,220 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 63,220 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 63,220 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday compared to 39,289 tonnes in the same period on Saturday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Sunday	Dec 21</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 7,226	17,039</p>
<p>    Import cargo		55,994	22,250</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, two ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, five are expected to sail and nine are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 30,000	 Al Safa		24/12</p>
<p>Soyoil		    5,360	 Champion Trader    22/12</p>
<p>Crude oil		68,000	 Capitan Mirinda    22/12</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 42,000	 Trade Resolve	25/12</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Bunga Selasih	28/12</p>
<p>Tallow		    3,137	 Alam Karang	  30/12</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
